   "id": "wired-and",
   "title": "Buffer function: two outputs on one pull-up",
   "page": 8,
   "description": "Two channels share a single pull-up resistor to a supply VPU, their outputs tied together. The common node is high only while both inputs are high; either input low pulls it down, so the node is the logical AND of the two inputs. The node feeds a microcontroller or further logic. Each input comes from a microcontroller or logic gate.",
